  </section>

  <details class="episode-details"><summary>About this paper</summary>
    <p>Streaming DiLoCo introduces three main improvements: streaming synchronization reduces peak bandwidth, overlapping communication with computation hides latency, and quantization compresses data exchanged between workers. The research shows similar performance to Data-Parallel training but with significantly reduced bandwidth, making it a promising approach for distributed LLM training.</p>
    
    
  </details>

  

